Figure 9.8: This client program receives a hostname and a textual message string as command line arguments. It connects to the server running on the specified host’s port 2718 and sends it a line of text containing the message. It then reads a reply line back and prints it out for the user to see.

For example, you could write an HTTP client or server in Java using this sort of code.
